283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (Across otherwise different incidents, four infrastructure surfaces recurred at the point where changes in agent behaviour became consequential actions.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (The evidence does not show that every interaction with an artificial actor is dangerous. It shows that the receiving environment often decides whether a behavioural deviation can produce a real effect. Authentication, reachability and executable capability answer whether an action can occur; they do not necessarily answer whether that action belongs to the current task.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (This distinction also helps explain why the incidents are difficult to reduce to a single model-side failure. The same model behaviour can have very different consequences depending on what credentials, routes, tools, approvals and environments are available when the trajectory changes.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
